{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3c41da4bca8ff1484e600e9efc2c4dad2abc3313e2b8296590a48ab76a38c38c","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI workflow / coverage reporting","key_entities":["_build-and-test.yml","coverage.xml","diff-cover","pytest-cov","--cov-report=xml","HEAD^","gerrit-refspec","GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY","test_ci_workflow_parity.py","_COVERAGE_FLAGS","ubuntu-latest","py3.13"],"problem_keywords":["diff-coverage","changed lines","coverage reporting","gerrit verification","report-only signal"],"propositions":["The default-suite pytest step on ubuntu+py3.13 must emit coverage.xml via --cov-report=xml:coverage.xml without affecting other matrix cells.","A report-only diff-cover step must run only on the Gerrit Verified lane (when gerrit-refspec is set) and compare against HEAD^ to surface changed-line coverage.","The diff-cover step must be non-blocking (--fail-under=0) and write results to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY in markdown format.","The step must skip gracefully on post-merge lanes and when coverage.xml is absent, with refspec passed via env variable to satisfy template-injection audit.","The CI workflow parity tests must pass with _COVERAGE_FLAGS updated across three embeddings in test_ci_workflow_parity.py."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787870440185271001,"uuid":"4e7c846e-7a78-4337-b90c-998800844aac"}